    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37651" root="لخ" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخَّتْ عَيْنُهُ</span></b> , (S, L, K,) aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلِخٌّ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخٌّ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخِيخٌ</span>, (L,) <i>His eye shed copious tears,</i> (S,
L, K,) <i>and its lids became rough.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخِخَتْ عَيْنُهُ</span>, as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَحِحَتْ</span>, <i>His eyelids stuck together, by reason of a white thick matter collected
in their corners.</i> (L.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لحّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخَّ فِى كَلَامِهِ</span>,
[aor., accord. to analogy, 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخِ3َ</span></b> ,] <i>He was obscure
and barbarous in his speech.</i> (K.)


